---@class posthog.signals.CheckSignalsScoutRecordResultRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field run_id string UUID of the `SignalScoutRun` bridge row.
---@field check_id string The check this run was dispatched to answer, as given in the run note.
---@field outcome posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckOutcomeEnum|string `passed` when the evidence meets the check's stated bar and the expectation holds, `failed` when the evidence meets the bar and the expectation does not hold. `inconclusive` when your tools worked but the evidence cannot settle the question; give a `reason`. `errored` only when a tool, query, or model call failed. Reserve `failed` for a conclusion, not a suspicion. * `passed` - Passed * `failed` - Failed * `errored` - Errored * `inconclusive` - Inconclusive
---@field reason? posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckInconclusiveReasonEnum|string|distilled.Null Required with `inconclusive`, and refused with any other outcome. `awaiting_data`: the data can still arrive (a rollout lag, a soak not complete, too few samples so far). `unmeasurable`: the data the check needs is not captured. `needs_manual_verification`: only a person or another environment can verify it. `no_fix_to_measure`: nothing was changed to fix the claim, so no window after a fix exists. A report resolved without a pull request still has a window that starts when it resolved. * `awaiting_data` - Awaiting Data * `unmeasurable` - Unmeasurable * `needs_manual_verification` - Needs Manual Verification * `no_fix_to_measure` - No Fix To Measure
---@field explanation string One or two sentences on what you looked at and what it showed. This is what a person reads on the report, so write it for them, with the numbers or entities you checked.
---@field observed_value? number|distilled.Null The number you measured, when the check came down to one. Leave it out otherwise.

