---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsActionsRunRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this signal report.
---@field action posthog.signals.ReportTaskActionKindEnum|string The action to run. Use a value from the actions list, or `ask` to send your own `message`. * `get_it_merged` - Get it merged * `make_it_green` - Make it green * `suggested_prompt` - Suggested prompt * `ask` - Ask
---@field suggested_prompt_index? number Required for `suggested_prompt`: the `suggested_prompt_index` from the actions list.
---@field message? string Your own request for the run. Required for `ask`, where it is the question or the work you want done on the report. Optional for `get_it_merged` and `make_it_green`, where it replaces the action's fixed request and keeps its instructions and gates: pass it when you know something the report does not, such as a merge order, a failure that is already on the base branch, or an expected conflict. Not accepted for `suggested_prompt`.

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsFeedbackRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this signal report.
---@field sentiment posthog.signals.SignalReportFeedbackSentimentEnum|string|distilled.Null The report rating: 'positive' (thumbs up), 'negative' (thumbs down), or null to clear it. * `positive` - positive * `negative` - negative
---@field note? string Free-form note explaining the rating. Capped at 4000 characters. Optional — a bare thumb carries none. When present and the report was authored by a scout, the note is forwarded to that scout as a steering note.

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsMergeRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this signal report.
---@field source_report_ids posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsMergeRequestSourceReportIdsList Ids of the duplicate reports to fold into this one (1–10). Each must be a live report in this project: a resolved, archived or deleted report is rejected with 409, as is the survivor's own id. Duplicates in the list are de-duplicated. The whole merge applies or none of it does.
---@field reason? string Optional one-line explanation of why these reports are the same issue. Recorded on each source's 'duplicate of' link and on the note left on the survivor. Capped at 500 characters.

---Ids of the duplicate reports to fold into this one (1–10). Each must be a live report in this project: a resolved, archived or deleted report is rejected with 409, as is the survivor's own id. Duplicates in the list are de-duplicated. The whole merge applies or none of it does.
---@alias posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsMergeRequestSourceReportIdsList string[]

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsRefundRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this signal report.
---@field reason posthog.signals.SignalReportRefundReasonEnum|string Why this PR is being refunded. One of: pr_incorrect (the PR doesn't address what the report promised), pr_not_useful (technically fine but not worth paying for), duplicate (covers work already charged elsewhere), other. Required — refund reviews key on it. * `pr_incorrect` - PR incorrect * `pr_not_useful` - PR not useful * `duplicate` - Duplicate * `other` - Other
---@field note? string Optional free-form context for the refund; stored on the refund and echoed in the report's dismissal artefact. Capped at 4000 characters.

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsReingestRequest
