---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsReviewersMeRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this signal report.
---@field removal_reason? posthog.signals.ReviewerRemovalReasonEnum|string Why the user steps off. 'wrong_area': the work should not be on them, for example they moved off the area or left the team. 'already_covered': someone else is on it. 'unavailable': they do not have bandwidth right now. 'other': explain in removal_note. Research reads the reason when it picks reviewers for later reports. * `wrong_area` - Not their area * `already_covered` - Someone else is on it * `unavailable` - No bandwidth * `other` - Other
---@field removal_note? string The user's own words for why, such as "I'm not on the payments team any more". Scouts read it when they route later reports.

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsReportsReviewersMeResponse

