---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsScoutNoteRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field content string The note's prose — feedback, a pointer, or a nudge for the scout(s) to weigh on their next runs (e.g. 'we shipped a new checkout on Tuesday, watch conversion closely', 'stop flagging the staging traffic spike'). Write it in Markdown; the run reads it verbatim.
---@field skill_name? string Address the note to one scout by its skill name (exact match against a configured scout on the project — check `scout-config-list` for the roster), or to one stage of the report pipeline by its reserved audience (`pipeline:report-research`); any other `pipeline:*` value is rejected. Use a pipeline audience for guidance about how reports get researched, judged, and routed rather than about what the scouts watch, so it reaches that stage and no scout. Omit or leave blank for a general note every scout sees.
---@field report_id? string|distilled.Null Optional id of the inbox report this note is about. The note then names the report so a scout can fetch it, and the report's activity log records that the note was left. Requires edit access to inbox reports, and the report must belong to this project. The report reference shares the note's character budget, so `content` is capped at 9938 characters when this is set.
---@field expires_at? string|distilled.Null Optional ISO-8601 expiry. After this time the note drops out of the default list view, so time-boxed steering ('watch closely this week') retires itself. Omit for a note that stays active until deleted. Best-effort — a value that can't be parsed or is already in the past is dropped (the note stays active), not rejected, so the note is never lost.

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsScoutReportCheckRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field run_id string UUID of the `SignalScoutRun` bridge row.
---@field title string Short label for the expectation, e.g. `Checkout 500s stay below 10 a day`.
---@field rationale? string Why the check is worth running.
---@field kind posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckKindEnum|string How the check is evaluated. * `metric_threshold` - Metric Threshold * `agent` - Agent
---@field config posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckConfig What the check measures and what the result must satisfy; the shape depends on `kind`.
---@field next_run_at? string When to first evaluate the check. Must be in the future and within 90 days. Defaults to 7 days from now.
---@field run_interval_minutes? number|distilled.Null Gap between runs for a recurring check, between 360 and 129600 minutes. Omit for a one-shot check.
---@field runs_remaining? number How many times to evaluate the check, at most 10. Defaults to 1.
---@field expires_at? string Horizon after which the check retires unrun. Defaults to 30 days after the last scheduled run, or the 90-day horizon if that comes first.
---@field report_id string The report the check attaches to.

---@class posthog.signals.CreateSignalsScoutRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
