---@class posthog.signals.EditReportResponse
---@field report_id string Id of the edited report.
---@field updated_fields posthog.signals.EditReportResponseUpdatedFieldsList Which presentation fields changed (e.g. `title`, `summary`); empty if only a note was appended.
---@field note_appended boolean Whether the edit included a note. True for a collapsed corroboration too, where the report's count moves and no work-log entry is written. Read `corroboration_collapsed` to tell the two apart.
---@field evidence_appended number How many observations this edit added to the report's evidence rail; 0 if none.
---@field links_appended number How many typed report-to-report links this edit wrote; 0 if none.
---@field source_issues_appended number How many source issues this edit added that the report did not name yet; 0 if none.
---@field reviewers_set boolean Whether the report's suggested reviewers were replaced.
---@field repository_set boolean Whether the report's repository was replaced (true for a cleared target too).
---@field repository string|distilled.Null The repository the report points at now, read back from the report rather than echoed from the request; null when the report has no target. Compare it with the `repository` you sent to confirm the correction landed.
---@field charts_set number|distilled.Null How many charts the report now shows, or null if the edit left its charts as they were (the field omitted, or a re-send of what was already stored). 0 means the edit took the report's charts down.
---@field metrics_set number|distilled.Null How many impact metrics the report now shows, or null when untouched/unchanged. 0 means the edit removed every metric.
---@field suggested_prompts_set number|distilled.Null How many prompts the report now suggests, or null if the edit left them as they were (the field omitted, or a re-send of what was already stored). 0 means the edit took the report's suggested prompts down.
---@field tags_set number|distilled.Null How many tags the report now carries, or null if the edit left them as they were (the field omitted, or a re-send of what was already stored). 0 means the edit removed the report's tags.
---@field is_content_revision boolean Whether this edit actually rewrote the report's title or summary. False for a note, a reviewer change, or a re-send of the text the report already had.
---@field content_revision_count number How many times a scout has rewritten this report's title or summary, counting this edit.
---@field supersedes_implementation boolean Whether the edit recorded that the report's pull request should be replaced. False when you did not ask for it, when the edit changed no content, or when the report has already been rewritten too many times.
---@field decision_fields_set posthog.signals.EditReportResponseDecisionFieldsSetList Which work decisions the edit replaced (`actionability`, `priority`). Empty when you set none, or re-sent the decisions the report already held.
---@field warnings posthog.signals.EditReportResponseWarningsList Request fields the edit did not apply, each with the reason. Empty when every field applied.
---@field corroboration_collapsed boolean Whether your note raised the report's corroboration count instead of landing as its own entry. Only notes marked corroboration_only can collapse; free-form notes remain in the work log.

---Which work decisions the edit replaced (`actionability`, `priority`). Empty when you set none, or re-sent the decisions the report already held.
---@alias posthog.signals.EditReportResponseDecisionFieldsSetList string[]

---Which presentation fields changed (e.g. `title`, `summary`); empty if only a note was appended.
---@alias posthog.signals.EditReportResponseUpdatedFieldsList string[]

---Request fields the edit did not apply, each with the reason. Empty when every field applied.
---@alias posthog.signals.EditReportResponseWarningsList posthog.signals.EditReportWarning[]

