---@field message string Why the field was not applied. The rest of the edit landed.

---@class posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field run_id string UUID of the `SignalScoutRun` bridge row.
---@field expected_reviewers? posthog.signals.ReviewerState Report reviewer_assignment.state read before selection began. Required when reviewer corrections are enabled.
---@field reviewer_outcome? posthog.signals.ReviewerSelectionOutcomeEnum|string A successful selection, a deliberate empty result, or an unavailable lookup. Defaults to selected when omitted. * `selected` - Selected * `no_suitable_owner` - No suitable owner * `lookup_failed` - Lookup failed
---@field reviewer_retry_reason? string Reason the reviewer lookup failed.
---@field reviewer_outcome_reason? string Why no suitable owner exists, with `reviewer_outcome: no_suitable_owner`. Required to clear a report that already has suggested reviewers: without it the current reviewers stay and the response carries a warning. The reason is recorded in the report's work log.
---@field report_id string Id of the report to edit (must belong to this project).
---@field title? string|distilled.Null Optional new title. Conventional-commit style (`type(scope): description`) renders with type/scope styling. The pipeline may later re-research and overwrite it.
---@field summary? string|distilled.Null Optional new summary. Markdown is supported (headings, lists, code, links; images are not rendered); lead with one plain declarative sentence — it becomes the inbox card headline. A heading, or a bold label on a line of its own with a blank line above it, marks a section that a threaded Slack delivery splits into its own reply. The pipeline may later re-research and overwrite it.
---@field append_note? string|distilled.Null Optional free-form note to append to the report's work log, attributed to this scout. Prefer it over rewriting a report you did not author: a note is additive and keeps the audit trail.
---@field corroboration_only? boolean Set only when `append_note` confirms the finding with no new information. The first four confirmations stay in the work log as entries; later ones only raise the report's corroboration count. Other notes always stay in the work log.
---@field append_evidence? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestAppendEvidenceList|distilled.Null Optional observations to add to the report's evidence rail, each becoming a bound signal attributed to this scout — adds to the report's evidence rather than replacing it. Use this for a new observation a reader should be able to check, and `append_note` for commentary (the owning team knows, a deploy fixed it). The report's signal count and weight move with the appended rows. Emit plus every append share a cap of 50 signals per report.
---@field suggested_reviewers? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestSuggestedReviewersList Optional reviewers to set on the report (each a `github_login` and/or `user_uuid`), replacing any existing list. Use this to route a report that surfaced with no reviewer — it re-runs autostart, so a report that was missing a qualifying reviewer can now open a draft PR. An empty list clears automatic reviewers when correction rules are enabled. Pins, exclusions, and confirmed lists are preserved. Pass expected_reviewers from the report reviewer_assignment.state read before selection.
---@field repository? string|distilled.Null Optional repository to point the report at, as `owner/repo` — the fix for a report that surfaced against the wrong codebase, so you correct it in place instead of filing a duplicate. It replaces the report's current target and re-runs autostart, so a report that had no repository to open a PR against can now open a draft PR. Omit the field to leave the target as it is, and pass the `NO_REPO` sentinel for a report where nothing under version control could change. The response's `repository` reads the target back from the report, and the call fails when the target you named did not land.
---@field charts? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestChartsList|distilled.Null The full set of charts the report should show. Replaces the report's charts rather than adding to them, the way `summary` replaces the summary — so read the report first and send every chart you want kept. Omit the field (or send null) to leave the report's existing charts untouched, and send an empty list to take them all down.
---@field metrics? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestMetricsList|distilled.Null The report's full impact-metric set, at most 6. Omit it or send null to keep the current set, send an empty list to clear it, or send the complete replacement. Mark one metric `primary` for the key observation and the rest `supporting`, for users, sessions, occurrences, conversion, latency, or revenue. Every metric needs a live `query`: an InsightVizNode wrapping one bounded TrendsQuery built only from EventsNode or ActionsNode sources, with at most 1000 estimated longitudinal points. An affected-users metric counts distinct people through one series with `math: dau`; never sum its buckets. A `value`/`value_at` snapshot is only an optional cached fallback, and a metric without a query is invalid.
---@field suggested_prompts? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestSuggestedPromptsList|distilled.Null The full set of follow-up prompts (questions or next-step actions) the report should offer above its `Ask AI` box. Replaces the report's prompts rather than adding to them, so send every one you want kept. Omit the field (or send null) to leave them untouched, and send an empty list to take them down, which is what you want once a rewrite has left them pointing at the old report.
---@field links? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestLinksList Typed, directed links from this report to others, recording how the work relates. Use `depends_on` when you split one finding into a stack and the second report's fix cannot land until the first one's does, so the order is recorded rather than left to a reader of the diffs. Additive: links join what the report already has rather than replacing them, and only this report gets a row, so link from the side the sentence starts at. Links of the same kind must stay acyclic and every report must be in this project.
---@field source_issues? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestSourceIssuesList The GitHub issues this report is about, when the finding came from an issue tracker. Pass the issue whenever the report is about one, so the report links back to it: a GitHub issue signal for the same issue then joins this report instead of opening a second one. When the project turned on GitHub issue comments, the issue gets one comment that links the report once its GitHub source ingests the issue. At most 5 per call. Additive: issues join the ones the report already names, and an issue it already names is skipped. Only a newly added issue gets a comment.
---@field tags? posthog.signals.EditSignalsScoutReportRequestTagsList|distilled.Null The report's full set of slug tags, at most 10. Replaces the report's tags rather than adding to them, so send every tag you want kept. Omit the field (or send null) to leave them untouched, and send an empty list to remove them. Reuse a slug the project already uses before you coin a new one.
---@field supersedes_implementation? boolean Set this only when your rewrite changes what the fix should be: a different root cause, a different file or layer, a materially wider or narrower scope. More evidence for the same fix is not a reason, because the report's open pull request already implements it: put that in `append_note`. Setting it true records a replacement decision for a ready report. Policy and eligibility checks gate the replacement. The existing pull request closes only after a successful, verified replacement. Technical failures retry automatically; policy blocks wait for a new edit or research trigger. Only honored alongside a `title` or `summary` that actually changes, and only within the first four content revisions, including revisions that did not request replacement. When the flag is not applied, `warnings` says why.
---@field actionability? posthog.signals.ActionabilityEnum|string|distilled.Null Optional new actionability call, for when new evidence changed your judgment. Replaces the report's actionability decision and re-runs autostart: `immediately_actionable` can open a draft PR, `requires_human_input` and `not_actionable` stop autostart from opening one. The report's inbox status does not change. Send it with `actionability_explanation`, and with `already_addressed` when the issue is handled, since the three replace the decision as one unit. * `immediately_actionable` - immediately_actionable * `requires_human_input` - requires_human_input * `not_actionable` - not_actionable
---@field actionability_explanation? string|distilled.Null 2-3 sentence evidence-grounded justification for `actionability`. Required when you set it.
---@field already_addressed? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the issue is already handled: fixed, or with a fix in flight. Part of the actionability decision, so it requires `actionability` and `actionability_explanation` too; omitted means false. Set it when a fix lands or starts, so autostart does not open a duplicate PR.
---@field priority? posthog.signals.AutonomyPriorityEnum|string|distilled.Null Optional new priority (`P0`-`P4`), for when the issue escalated or eased. Replaces the report's priority and re-runs autostart, which needs a priority to open a draft PR. Requires `priority_explanation`. * `P0` - P0 * `P1` - P1 * `P2` - P2 * `P3` - P3 * `P4` - P4
---@field priority_explanation? string|distilled.Null 2-3 sentence justification for `priority`. Required when `priority` is set.

