---@class posthog.signals.GetSignalsReportsForMeRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field focus? string Free text about what to put first, such as `error tracking` or `billing reports`. A request with focus always starts a new build, and an unfocused request never reuses it. Pass `wait_seconds` to wait for it.
---@field limit? number The most reports to return, best first. Defaults to 25. Values above the configured maximum (50) use the maximum.
---@field max_age_minutes? number The oldest `checked_at` you accept. When the stored list is older, the request reads every candidate report, which can take some seconds, and starts a build if your inbox changed. Leave it out to get the stored list quickly. A new report then joins the list at the next scheduled build.
---@field refresh? boolean Start a new build even when the stored one is current. The build runs in the background, so the response has `building: true`. Pass `wait_seconds` to wait for it.
---@field wait_seconds? number When the request starts a build or one is running, wait for its list until this many seconds after the request started. Defaults to 0, which does not wait. A build usually takes 10 to 60 seconds.

---@class posthog.signals.GetSignalsReportsRefundSummaryRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.

---@class posthog.signals.GetSignalsReportsSectionCountRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field actionability? string Comma-separated actionability judgments to include. Valid values: immediately_actionable, requires_human_input, not_actionable. Reports without a judgment are excluded.
---@field already_addressed? boolean Filter by whether the latest actionability judgment says the issue is already being handled. False also includes older reports where that judgment did not record a value.
---@field assignee? posthog.signals.GetSignalsReportsSectionCountRequestAssignee|string 'me' returns reports claimed by exactly the requesting actor: the user, the internal task, or the MCP agent. 'mine' returns every report the requesting user claimed: their own claims and claims by MCP agents acting for them. Internal task claims are not included.
---@field channel_id? string Narrow to reports assigned to one space (channel). Absent or empty means all reports regardless of assignment.
---@field created_after? string ISO 8601 datetime. Keeps reports created at or after this time.
---@field created_before? string ISO 8601 datetime. Keeps reports created before this time. Use it for reports older than a cutoff, instead of reading every page.
---@field exclude? posthog.signals.GetSignalsReportsSectionCountRequestExcludeList Report ids to leave out of the results and counts, for example the reports a client already shows, as repeated parameters or comma-separated. The other reports keep their order. At most 100.
---@field include_unlisted? boolean Include reports kept out of the shared inbox. A report is kept out when the scout that authored it turned off its `inbox` output destination. Defaults to false. Fetching a report by id always works, whatever this value is.
---@field priority? string Comma-separated list of priorities to include. Valid values: P0, P1, P2, P3, P4. Reports without a priority assignment are excluded when this filter is set.
---@field ranking_min_lift? string Comma-separated <outcome>:<lift> pairs, e.g. fix:2,open:1.5. Keeps reports whose served ranking lift is at least the value for every named outcome. Outcomes: open, action, fix. Read inbox-ranking-outcomes-list for what each outcome means. Unscored and stale reports never match. Needs staff or the inbox model sort rollout: other users get a 400.
---@field ranking_min_probability? string Comma-separated <outcome>:<probability> pairs, e.g. fix:0.3. Keeps reports whose served ranking probability is at least the value for every named outcome. Outcomes: open, action, fix. Read inbox-ranking-outcomes-list for what each outcome means. Unscored and stale reports never match. Needs staff or the inbox model sort rollout: other users get a 400.
---@field scope? string Reviewer scope: for_me, entire_project, or teammate. Pass teammate_uuid with teammate.
---@field scout? string Comma-separated list of scout skill_name slugs (e.g. signals-scout-error-tracking). Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals was authored by one of these scouts. Combines with source_product as an AND.
---@field scout_prefix? string Scout skill_name prefix (e.g. signals-scout-customer-analytics). Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals was authored by a scout whose skill_name starts with this prefix — new scouts in the family match without callers listing every name. Combines with the other filters as an AND.
---@field search? string Case-insensitive substring match against report title and summary.
---@field source_id? string Comma-separated list of source record ids. Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals came from one of these records — e.g. pass a support ticket's UUID to see what the inbox already found for that ticket. Requires exactly one source_product, since a source id is only unique within its product.
---@field source_product? string Comma-separated list of source products to include. Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals comes from one of these products (e.g. error_tracking, session_replay).
---@field suggested_reviewers? string Comma-separated list of PostHog user UUIDs. Reports are kept if their suggested reviewers include any of the given users.
---@field task_id? string Only reports associated with this task (via the report's task associations).
---@field teammate_uuid? string PostHog user UUID used when scope=teammate.
---@field unclaimed? boolean Filter by whether the report has no owner and no draft, open, or unknown PR. Resolved reports are never unclaimed.
---@field unread? boolean Filter by the current user's report read state.
---@field use_priority_preference? boolean When true and priority is omitted, include priorities at or above the requesting user's personal PR-generation threshold, falling back to the project threshold.

