---@class posthog.signals.ListSignalsReportsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field actionability? string Comma-separated actionability judgments to include. Valid values: immediately_actionable, requires_human_input, not_actionable. Reports without a judgment are excluded.
---@field already_addressed? boolean Filter by whether the latest actionability judgment says the issue is already being handled. False also includes older reports where that judgment did not record a value.
---@field assignee? posthog.signals.ListSignalsReportsRequestAssignee|string 'me' returns reports claimed by exactly the requesting actor: the user, the internal task, or the MCP agent. 'mine' returns every report the requesting user claimed: their own claims and claims by MCP agents acting for them. Internal task claims are not included.
---@field channel_id? string Narrow to reports assigned to one space (channel). Absent or empty means all reports regardless of assignment.
---@field count_only? boolean Return the filtered total with an empty results page. Skips report ordering, serialization, and decorative metadata lookups. Defaults to false.
---@field created_after? string ISO 8601 datetime. Keeps reports created at or after this time.
---@field created_before? string ISO 8601 datetime. Keeps reports created before this time. Use it for reports older than a cutoff, instead of reading every page.
---@field exclude? posthog.signals.ListSignalsReportsRequestExcludeList Report ids to leave out of the results and counts, for example the reports a client already shows, as repeated parameters or comma-separated. The other reports keep their order. At most 100.
---@field has_implementation_pr? boolean Filter reports by whether an implementation pull request is attached. 'true' keeps only reports with a PR; 'false' keeps only those without. Pair with count_only=true to return only the filtered total.
---@field include_all_statuses? boolean When true, the list includes reports in every status with no default exclusions applied — currently that adds suppressed (dismissed) reports, which are otherwise hidden. Use it to see the full inbox state (e.g. deduplicating before creating a report) and read each row's status (plus dismissal_reason/dismissal_note on dismissed rows) before acting. Deleted reports are terminal and never returned. Defaults to false, which keeps the existing default exclusions. Ignored when an explicit 'status' filter is set — that filter alone decides which statuses are returned.
---@field include_source_metadata? boolean Fill `source_products` and `scout_name` on each row. These come from ClickHouse, so pass false to skip that lookup and get the page from Postgres only: rows then carry an empty `source_products` and a null `scout_name`. Load them after with `source_metadata`. Defaults to true.
---@field include_unlisted? boolean Include reports kept out of the shared inbox. A report is kept out when the scout that authored it turned off its `inbox` output destination. Defaults to false. Fetching a report by id always works, whatever this value is.
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field ordering? string Comma-separated ordering clauses. Each clause is a field name optionally prefixed with '-' for descending. Allowed fields: status, is_suggested_reviewer, signal_count, total_weight, priority, created_at, updated_at, id, ranking_open, ranking_action, ranking_fix. Defaults to '-is_suggested_reviewer,status,-updated_at'. Each ranking_<outcome> field sorts by the served ranking model's probability for that public outcome, with unscored reports last in either direction. Read inbox-ranking-outcomes-list for what each outcome means. The ranking fields need staff or the inbox model sort rollout: other users get a 400.
---@field priority? string Comma-separated list of priorities to include. Valid values: P0, P1, P2, P3, P4. Reports without a priority assignment are excluded when this filter is set.
---@field ranking_id? string For sort=personal: the ranking_id of the first page. Pass it on later pages, so a new personal ranking does not reorder them. When that ranking no longer exists, the latest one applies.
---@field ranking_min_lift? string Comma-separated <outcome>:<lift> pairs, e.g. fix:2,open:1.5. Keeps reports whose served ranking lift is at least the value for every named outcome. Outcomes: open, action, fix. Read inbox-ranking-outcomes-list for what each outcome means. Unscored and stale reports never match. Needs staff or the inbox model sort rollout: other users get a 400.
---@field ranking_min_probability? string Comma-separated <outcome>:<probability> pairs, e.g. fix:0.3. Keeps reports whose served ranking probability is at least the value for every named outcome. Outcomes: open, action, fix. Read inbox-ranking-outcomes-list for what each outcome means. Unscored and stale reports never match. Needs staff or the inbox model sort rollout: other users get a 400.
---@field scope? string Reviewer scope: for_me, entire_project, or teammate. Pass teammate_uuid with teammate.
---@field scout? string Comma-separated list of scout skill_name slugs (e.g. signals-scout-error-tracking). Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals was authored by one of these scouts. Combines with source_product as an AND.
---@field scout_prefix? string Scout skill_name prefix (e.g. signals-scout-customer-analytics). Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals was authored by a scout whose skill_name starts with this prefix — new scouts in the family match without callers listing every name. Combines with the other filters as an AND.
---@field search? string Case-insensitive substring match against report title and summary.
---@field sort? string Inbox sort preset: priority, recommended, personal, last_updated, newest, or oldest. Ignored when ordering is supplied. recommended resolves per user to a ranker: the priority order, or the open, action or fix outcome of the served ranking model, highest score first, with unscored and stale reports in priority order after the scored ones. The response's ranker field names the one used, and its ranking_pill field says whether to show score pills. personal puts the reports of your stored personal ranking first, by rank, then the reports it folded, then every other report in your recommended order. It only reads the stored ranking and never starts a build. With no stored personal ranking, it is the recommended order.
---@field source_id? string Comma-separated list of source record ids. Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals came from one of these records — e.g. pass a support ticket's UUID to see what the inbox already found for that ticket. Requires exactly one source_product, since a source id is only unique within its product.
---@field source_product? string Comma-separated list of source products to include. Reports are kept if at least one of their contributing signals comes from one of these products (e.g. error_tracking, session_replay).
---@field status? string Comma-separated list of statuses to include. Valid values: potential, candidate, in_progress, pending_input, ready, resolved, failed, suppressed. Defaults to all statuses except suppressed.
---@field suggested_reviewers? string Comma-separated list of PostHog user UUIDs. Reports are kept if their suggested reviewers include any of the given users.
---@field task_id? string Only reports associated with this task (via the report's task associations).
---@field teammate_uuid? string PostHog user UUID used when scope=teammate.
---@field unclaimed? boolean Filter by whether the report has no owner and no draft, open, or unknown PR. Resolved reports are never unclaimed.
---@field unread? boolean Filter by the current user's report read state.
---@field use_priority_preference? boolean When true and priority is omitted, include priorities at or above the requesting user's personal PR-generation threshold, falling back to the project threshold.
---@field view? string Apply an inbox view: actionable, for_you, needs_input, needs_decision, monitoring, resolved, dismissed, held_back, not_actionable, or all. Each view applies the corresponding status, actionability, and implementation-PR filters. for_you holds the open, actionable reports that wait for the requesting user's input, that they claimed, or that name them as a suggested reviewer. needs_decision also includes failed reports without a judgment. dismissed and held_back split the suppressed reports: dismissed holds the ones a person or agent dismissed, merged, or whose pull request closed without merging; held_back holds the ones the safety or actionability judge suppressed before anyone saw them. Each row's suppression_source says which.

