---A deterministic check: measure one number, compare it, record the verdict.
---
---The number comes either from a metric the report already shows (``metric_id``) or from a query
---the author supplies. Both end up in the same runner, so a supplied query must satisfy the live
---metric contract — the node allowlist, the bounded window, and the single-output-series rule.
---
---A caller names one source. When it names a metric, the create path copies that metric's query
---into ``query`` before the row is stored, so the check keeps measuring what its author saw even if
---the report's metric is later rewritten under the same id; ``metric_id`` stays as provenance.
---
---Unknown keys are refused rather than ignored, so a misspelled field name is reported instead of
---being dropped in silence and stored as it arrived.
---@class posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfig
---@field metric_id? string|distilled.Null Identifier of a metric on the report whose query this check measures. The metric's query is copied into `query` when the check is created.
---@field query? posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfigQueryMap|distilled.Null Live InsightVizNode wrapping one TrendsQuery: supplied by the caller, or copied from the named metric when the check is created. `dateRange.date_from` must be a relative window such as `-13d`, and `date_to` must be empty, so the check measures the days before each run rather than the days before it was written. The query must produce exactly one output series: use one event or action series, or combine up to ten of them with exactly one formula. Use no breakdown and no compare mode. A `trendsFilter.display` of `Metric` turns compare mode on, so `metricShowChange` is switched off for you unless `metricSummary` is `latest`, which keeps compare mode off already.
---@field monitoring? posthog.signals.MonitoringMetricConfig|distilled.Null Optional Monitoring measurement definition, available only with the organization's Monitoring rollout. Measurements cover Monitoring start through the observation time. Omit for existing whole-window checks.
---@field comparison posthog.signals.CheckComparison What the measured value must satisfy to pass.
---@field baseline_value? number|distilled.Null The value observed when the check was written, recorded on each result for context.
---@field metric_kind? posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfigMetricKind|string|distilled.Null How to draw this measurement; copied from a referenced metric.
---@field value_format? posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfigValueFormat|string|distilled.Null How to format measured values; copied from a referenced metric.
---@field unit? string|distilled.Null Optional value suffix.

---@alias posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfigMetricKind "affected_users"|"affected_sessions"|"occurrences"|"conversion_rate"|"error_rate"|"duration"|"revenue"|"custom"

---@alias posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfigQueryMap { [string]: any }

---@alias posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfigValueFormat "number"|"count"|"percentage"|"percentage_scaled"|"duration"|"currency"

