---@class posthog.signals.MonitoringMetricConfig
---@field purpose? posthog.signals.MonitoringMetricConfigPurposeEnum|string `expectation` evaluates whether the implementation met its target. `minimum_evidence` checks a fixed minimum sample count: meeting it passes the guard; missing it is inconclusive and requires assessment, never an implementation failure. Use a positive whole-number `gte` target on one unsampled raw count.
---@field reference_period_minutes number The period the comparison target describes, in minutes. Independent of the soak and run schedule.
---@field threshold_scaling posthog.signals.ThresholdScalingEnum|string How the target applies to a measurement from Monitoring start to the observation time. `linear` multiplies the target by elapsed minutes / reference_period_minutes and requires an additive event count or property sum. `fixed` keeps the target unchanged, including for rates and averages. This definition does not enable Monitoring execution.
---@field baseline_period_minutes? number|distilled.Null The actual period measured by baseline_value, in minutes. Required when a baseline is supplied.

---@alias posthog.signals.MonitoringMetricConfigPurposeEnum "expectation"|"minimum_evidence"

