---@class posthog.signals.PersonalRanking
---@field status posthog.signals.PersonalRankingStatusEnum ready: the list is in `results`. unavailable: personal ranking is off now, and `results` is empty. * `ready` - ready * `unavailable` - unavailable
---@field personalized boolean True when the language model ranked the list with your activity summary. False when you have no summary yet or the build fell back to the inbox order.
---@field cached boolean True when the list is a stored one. False when it is the inbox order fallback or the new list that `wait_seconds` waited for.
---@field stale boolean True when the list does not match your current inbox or focus. When `building` is true, a newer list is on the way. Otherwise a report in the list changed since the build, and the next scheduled build updates it. Pass `refresh` for a new list now.
---@field building boolean True when a new list is being built in the background. Call again in a few seconds, or pass `wait_seconds`, to get it.
---@field fallback_reason string|distilled.Null Why the list is in inbox order and not ranked by the language model. building: no list is stored yet and one is being built. rate_limited: no list is stored yet and a build limit was reached, either yours or the shared daily one. build_failed: no list is stored yet and the build could not start. no_activity_summary: you have no activity summary yet, so the model did not rank the list. llm_error, timeout, malformed_output, truncated_output, no_candidates or ai_not_approved: the stored build fell back. Null when the model ranked it.
---@field generated_at string|distilled.Null When the list was built.
---@field checked_at string|distilled.Null When a build or a check last compared the list with your full inbox. The list is current as at this time. Null when no list is stored.
---@field latency_ms number|distilled.Null How long the model call of the build took, in ms. Null when there was no model call.
---@field activity_summary_version number|distilled.Null The version of your activity summary that the build read, or null.
---@field candidates_considered number How many reports the build considered.
---@field ranked_count number How many reports the stored list ranks. `results` holds at most `limit` of them.
