---One chart attached to a report — rendered in the inbox and referenceable from the summary.
---@class posthog.signals.ReportChart
---@field chart_id string Stable slug for this chart within the report (lowercase letters, numbers, underscores, hyphens; must start with a letter or number). Reference it from `summary` as a markdown link with a `chart:` target — `[Daily signups](chart:signups-drop)` — to place the chart at that point in the body. A chart you don't reference still renders, below the summary.
---@field title string Short heading shown above the chart.
---@field query any The query node to render. `kind` must be `InsightVizNode` (an ad-hoc product analytics chart), `DataVisualizationNode` (a SQL series — a `HogQLQuery` source plus a `display`), or `SavedInsightNode` (an existing insight by `shortId`). Pin the window to absolute dates where the node supports it, so the reader sees the data you wrote about rather than whatever a relative range resolves to when they open the report.
---@field caption? string|distilled.Null Optional one-line note on what to look at in the chart.
---@field size? posthog.signals.SizeEnum|string|distilled.Null How much height the chart gets: `small` for a single number or a short series, `medium` for an ordinary graph, `large` when there are rows or a grid to read (retention, paths, a wide breakdown). Leave it out unless the default looks wrong — the inbox sizes a chart from its query, and two charts referenced from the same paragraph sit side by side. * `small` - small * `medium` - medium * `large` - large

---One observation backing an authored report — becomes a bound signal row on the report.
---@class posthog.signals.ReportEvidence
---@field description string Prose for this observation. Embedded and rendered to the safety/research surfaces.
---@field source_id string Stable id for this observation within the report (lets a later edit address it).

---* `depends_on` - Depends on
---* `part_of` - Part of
---* `follow_up_of` - Follow-up of
---* `duplicate_of` - Duplicate of
---* `recurrence_of` - Recurrence of
---@alias posthog.signals.ReportLinkKindEnum "depends_on"|"part_of"|"follow_up_of"|"duplicate_of"|"recurrence_of"

---One typed, directed link to write on the report being emitted or edited.
---@class posthog.signals.ReportLinkWrite
---@field kind posthog.signals.ReportLinkKindEnum|string How this report relates to `report_id`. `depends_on` for work that cannot land until the other report's fix does, `part_of` for one piece of a larger report, `follow_up_of` for work the other report left behind, `duplicate_of` for the same problem filed twice, and `recurrence_of` for a problem a resolved report already covered. * `depends_on` - Depends on * `part_of` - Part of * `follow_up_of` - Follow-up of * `duplicate_of` - Duplicate of * `recurrence_of` - Recurrence of
---@field report_id string Id of the report to link to. Must be another report in this project.
---@field reason? string Optional one-line note on why the reports are linked this way.

---One impact measurement shown on a report.
---@class posthog.signals.ReportMetric
---@field metric_id string Stable slug for this metric within the report: lowercase letters, numbers, underscores, and hyphens, starting with a letter or number.
---@field title string Short human-readable label for the measurement.
---@field kind posthog.signals.ReportMetricKindEnum What the value measures, independent of how it is formatted or drawn. * `affected_users` - affected_users * `affected_sessions` - affected_sessions * `occurrences` - occurrences * `conversion_rate` - conversion_rate * `error_rate` - error_rate * `duration` - duration * `revenue` - revenue * `custom` - custom
---@field role? posthog.signals.RoleEnum `primary` for the report's key observation, otherwise `supporting`. * `primary` - primary * `supporting` - supporting
---@field value? number|distilled.Null Latest saved snapshot, initially observed during authoring and replaced when a person opens the inbox or the report. Null means no snapshot is available to this viewer; it never means zero. The required live query remains the source of truth.
---@field value_at? string|distilled.Null When the visible snapshot value was measured; null when value is null.
---@field series? posthog.signals.ReportMetricSeriesList|distilled.Null Trailing per-bucket values of the live query, oldest first, saved with the value snapshot so a list row can draw the trend without running the query; at most 14 points. Null when no snapshot series is available to this viewer.
---@field value_format? posthog.signals.ValueFormatEnum How to format the numeric value; semantic meaning remains in kind. `percentage` uses percentage points, so 34 renders as 34%; `percentage_scaled` uses a 0–1 ratio, so 0.34 renders as 34%. Sessions and occurrences use count; duration uses duration with an ms/s unit; revenue uses currency with an ISO currency unit. * `number` - number * `count` - count * `percentage` - percentage * `percentage_scaled` - percentage_scaled * `duration` - duration * `currency` - currency
---@field unit? string|distilled.Null Optional short suffix or currency code, such as `users`, `ms`, or `USD`.
---@field query? any Required when authoring: a live InsightVizNode wrapping one bounded TrendsQuery. Consumers derive a BoldNumber execution for the whole-window aggregate and an ActionsBar execution for longitudinal buckets. The query must produce exactly one output series and no more than 1000 estimated longitudinal points; one formula may combine up to ten event or action source series. An affected_users metric uses exactly one source with `math: dau`; never sum its per-bucket unique-user values. A response omits this on list or redacts it to null on detail when the viewer lacks access to the definition.
---@field caption? string|distilled.Null Optional context the tile cannot show, such as a filter that narrows the count or a caveat on the data. Omit it rather than restate the title, unit, or window.
---@field goal_value? number|distilled.Null Proposed threshold after release. Informational only; does not schedule a check.
---@field goal_direction? posthog.signals.GoalDirectionEnum|distilled.Null Whether success means at most or at least goal_value. * `at_most` - at_most * `at_least` - at_least
---@field goal_grain? posthog.signals.GoalGrainEnum Whether the goal compares with the whole query window or each chart bucket. * `whole_window` - whole_window * `per_interval` - per_interval
---@field decision_window_days? number|distilled.Null Suggested days after release before assessing impact, not a monitoring schedule.
---@field minimum_data_points? number|distilled.Null Optional number of qualifying observations before assessing impact.

---@class posthog.signals.ReportMetricComparison
---@field value number Baseline or previous value, formatted like the current value.
---@field label string Short context for the comparison, such as `Previous period`.

---* `affected_users` - affected_users
---* `affected_sessions` - affected_sessions
---* `occurrences` - occurrences
---* `conversion_rate` - conversion_rate
---* `error_rate` - error_rate
---* `duration` - duration
---* `revenue` - revenue
---* `custom` - custom
---@alias posthog.signals.ReportMetricKindEnum "affected_users"|"affected_sessions"|"occurrences"|"conversion_rate"|"error_rate"|"duration"|"revenue"|"custom"

