---@class posthog.signals.ScoutFleetEntry
---@field skill_name string The skill this config schedules as a scout.
---@field run_interval_minutes number Minutes between runs when no cron schedule is set (default 1440, every 24 hours).
---@field run_cron_schedule string|distilled.Null Optional cron expression, evaluated in the project timezone. Takes precedence over the interval.
---@field emit boolean Whether this scout's findings actually reach the inbox. False means dry-run: it runs and logs but emits nothing, so its silence says nothing about the surface it watches.
---@field last_run_at string|distilled.Null ISO-8601 timestamp the coordinator last dispatched this scout, or null if it has never run.
---@field last_emitted_at string|distilled.Null ISO-8601 timestamp this scout last produced output on either channel (a finding, or an authored/edited report), within `emitted_lookback_days`. Null means quiet for at least that window, not never.
---@field not_running_reason string|distilled.Null Why this scout is in the `disabled` bucket: `turned_off` (a person or seed posture set it off), `auto_paused` (the system paused it), or `skill_unavailable` (left on, but its skill was deleted, superseded, or withheld, so it never dispatches). Null for scouts that actually run.
