---These are the values the coordinator actually applies at dispatch (resolved per-team override →
---fleet-wide default → code constant), so the UI can show the real throttle rather than what a
---user thinks they configured.
---@class posthog.signals.ScoutLimits
---@field max_runs_per_tick number Most scout runs the team can start in a single 30-minute coordinator tick.
---@field max_runs_per_day number|distilled.Null Most scout runs the team can start per rolling 24 hours, or null when uncapped.
---@field runs_today number Scout runs the team has started in the trailing 24 hours.
---@field runs_remaining_today number|distilled.Null Runs still allowed in the trailing 24h window (max_runs_per_day − runs_today), or null when uncapped.
---@field max_enabled_scouts number Most scouts the project can have switched on at once. Enabling another past this is rejected.

---One project member's routing identity, for picking a `suggested_reviewers` entry on a report.
---@class posthog.signals.ScoutMember
---@field user_uuid string The member's stable PostHog user UUID — the same id that appears as `created_by.uuid` on entities they own. A durable handle for this person across runs.
---@field email string The member's email — use to match a finding's owner by name/email.
---@field first_name string The member's first name (may be empty).
---@field last_name string The member's last name (may be empty).
---@field github_login string|distilled.Null The member's resolved GitHub login (lowercased), already resolved server-side. Null when the member has no linked GitHub account, which does not stop you routing to them: pass their `user_uuid` in `suggested_reviewers` and the report reaches them. A null login only means no draft PR can be opened as that person.
---@field teams posthog.signals.ScoutMemberTeamsList The teams this member is on, from the project's synced team roster. Empty when no roster is synced, or when the member has no linked GitHub account, since the roster is keyed on that login. The roster is a periodic snapshot, so it can lag the live team.
---@field activity? posthog.signals.ScoutMemberActivity|distilled.Null What the member worked on recently. Use it as context to check against the report, not as proof: general activity is not evidence that the member owns the affected work. Filled only when the call passes `search` or `team` and returns at most 10 members. Null when the member has no ready summary, or when activity summaries are not available for this project.

---What one member worked on recently, from their activity summary.
---@class posthog.signals.ScoutMemberActivity
---@field headline string|distilled.Null One line about the member's recent work.
---@field themes posthog.signals.ScoutMemberActivityThemesList The labels of the main threads of the member's recent work.
---@field owned posthog.signals.ScoutMemberActivityOwnedList Up to 5 objects the member created or changed, the most edited first.
---@field watched posthog.signals.ScoutMemberActivityWatchedList Up to 5 objects the member opened on several days, the most opened first. A member who only reads the work shows up here. A specific object here can support a reviewer pick when the pick's `reason` names it.
