---One MCP tool, with what a scout would need to call it.
---@class posthog.signals.ScoutToolCatalogueEntry
---@field name string The tool's permanent identifier, for example `insight-get`. This is the name a scout calls.
---@field title string The label people read, for example `Get insight`.
---@field summary string One line on what the tool does. The tool's full description runs to several kilobytes on some tools, so it is not part of this listing.
---@field category string The product area the tool belongs to, for example `Error tracking`. Use it to group the listing.
---@field feature string The feature key the MCP server filters on, for example `error_tracking`. Narrower than `category`.
---@field required_scopes posthog.signals.ScoutToolCatalogueEntryRequiredScopesList The API scopes a token must carry to call the tool. Empty for a tool that needs none.
---@field is_read_only boolean True when the tool only reads. A false value means the tool can change the project's data.
---@field requires_ai_consent boolean True when the tool is hidden until the project consents to AI features.
---@field holdable boolean True when a scout run can hold every scope the tool requires. A false value means no scout reaches the tool, whatever it is granted, so it cannot be configured for one.
---@field missing_scopes posthog.signals.ScoutToolCatalogueEntryMissingScopesList Required scopes the baseline `signals_scout` preset does not carry. On a holdable tool these are what the scout has to be granted, or the preset it has to opt into. On a tool that is not holdable they include every scope no scout can reach, and can also include scopes a person can grant. Compare them with `grantable_write_scopes` and `presets` to tell the two apart.
---@field feature_flag string|distilled.Null Feature flag key that gates the tool, or null when the tool is always served. The flag resolves per project, so evaluate it for the project you are configuring before you offer the tool.
---@field feature_flag_behavior string|distilled.Null How `feature_flag` gates the tool: `enable` (served only while the flag is on) or `disable` (served only while the flag is off). Null means the default, `enable`.
---@field feature_flag_variant string|distilled.Null Variant of `feature_flag` the tool needs, or null when any truthy value serves it.
---@field hidden_when_flag_on string|distilled.Null A second flag key that hides the tool while it is on, independent of `feature_flag`. Usually null.
---@field feature_entitlement string|distilled.Null Plan feature the organization must have for the tool to be served, or null when the tool is free.

---Required scopes the baseline `signals_scout` preset does not carry. On a holdable tool these are what the scout has to be granted, or the preset it has to opt into. On a tool that is not holdable they include every scope no scout can reach, and can also include scopes a person can grant. Compare them with `grantable_write_scopes` and `presets` to tell the two apart.
---@alias posthog.signals.ScoutToolCatalogueEntryMissingScopesList string[]

