---@class posthog.signals.SearchSignalsScoutScratchpadRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field content_max_chars? number Truncate each entry's `content` to the first N characters (a preview). Omit for the full body. Ignored when `keys_only=true`.
---@field date_from? string ISO-8601 inclusive lower bound on `updated_at`. Omit to skip the lower bound.
---@field date_to? string ISO-8601 exclusive upper bound on `updated_at`. Pass to walk back past the result cap on subsequent calls (cursor-style: set to the `updated_at` of the oldest entry from the prior page).
---@field include_expired? boolean Include entries whose `expires_at` has passed. Off by default so a time-boxed memory retires itself; turn it on to audit what the fleet remembered and when it lapsed.
---@field key? string Exact key match — returns the single entry with this key, or nothing. Use this to re-read a known entry; `text` searches key *and* content, so it can push the row you asked for past the limit.
---@field keys_only? boolean When true, blank each entry's `content` and return only keys + metadata. Use to scan which memories exist without pulling their (potentially large) bodies, then re-query the ones worth a full read. Takes precedence over `content_max_chars`.
---@field limit? number Max rows to return (default 20, hard cap 1000).
---@field skill_name? string Return only the entries this writer created, matched against `created_by_skill` (a scout skill name or a `pipeline:*` identity). Omit to return entries from every writer.
---@field text? string ILIKE substring match against `content` and `key`. Must contain 3 letters or digits in a row, or 2 next to a symbol such as `ai_` or `pr:`. Omit to return the most recent entries.

---@alias posthog.signals.SearchSignalsScoutScratchpadResponseBodyList posthog.signals.ScratchpadEntry[]

