---@class posthog.signals.SignalReportCheck
---@field id string
---@field title string Short label for the expectation, e.g. `Checkout 500s stay below 10 a day`.
---@field rationale string Why the author set the check.
---@field kind posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckKindEnum How the check is evaluated. * `metric_threshold` - Metric Threshold * `agent` - Agent
---@field status posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckStatusEnum `pending` while the check waits for the report to resolve, `active` while it still runs; every other value is terminal. * `pending` - Pending * `active` - Active * `passed` - Passed * `failed` - Failed * `errored` - Errored * `inconclusive` - Inconclusive * `expired` - Expired * `cancelled` - Cancelled
---@field config posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckConfig What the check measures and what the result must satisfy; the shape depends on `kind`. `query` and `baseline_value` are null when you cannot read the data they describe.
---@field monitoring_timing? posthog.signals.MonitoringCheckTiming|distilled.Null Server-derived timing for open checks on Monitoring reports, including archived Monitoring periods. Omitted when Monitoring is disabled or the check is outside that lane.
---@field approved_at string|distilled.Null
---@field next_run_at string Stored coordinator schedule, provisional while pending. During Monitoring this can be the observation-window end rather than another measurement; use `monitoring_timing` for interim timing.
---@field soak_minutes number|distilled.Null This check's observation window during Monitoring, in minutes. Otherwise the minimum wait after resolution; metric checks also wait for a full post-resolution query window. Null on legacy checks.
---@field run_interval_minutes number|distilled.Null Gap between interim Monitoring measurements or recurring verdicts. Null uses the Monitoring executor's default cadence, otherwise denotes a one-shot check.
---@field runs_remaining number Terminal evaluations still owed before the check retires as passed. Interim Monitoring observations do not consume this count.
---@field expires_at string Horizon after which the check retires without running again.
---@field last_run_at string|distilled.Null When the check last ran; null before its first run.
---@field last_outcome posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckOutcomeEnum|distilled.Null Verdict of the most recent run. * `passed` - Passed * `failed` - Failed * `errored` - Errored * `inconclusive` - Inconclusive
---@field last_outcome_reason posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckInconclusiveReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why the most recent run could not settle the claim. Set only when `last_outcome` is `inconclusive`: `awaiting_data`, `unmeasurable`, `needs_manual_verification`, or `no_fix_to_measure`. * `awaiting_data` - Awaiting Data * `unmeasurable` - Unmeasurable * `needs_manual_verification` - Needs Manual Verification * `no_fix_to_measure` - No Fix To Measure
---@field dispatched_at string|distilled.Null When the `agent` check's scout run started, cleared as soon as a verdict is recorded. A non-null value is what tells a reader the check is running rather than waiting, because dispatch also pushes `next_run_at` out to the result window. Always null on a `metric_threshold` check, which is measured in the tick that collects it.
---@field consecutive_errors number Runs that could not be measured since the last clean one.
---@field created_at string
---@field updated_at string

---@alias posthog.signals.SignalReportCheckConfig posthog.signals.MetricThresholdConfig|posthog.signals.AgentCheckConfig

