---@class posthog.signals.SignalReportList
---@field id string
---@field title string|distilled.Null
---@field summary string|distilled.Null
---@field summary_lead string The opening of `summary` as plain text on one line: the text before its first section heading, with chart links removed and other links reduced to their text. At most 450 characters.
---@field reviewer_assignment posthog.signals.ReviewerControlResponse|distilled.Null Reviewer control and state token for preparing an automatic proposal.
---@field status posthog.signals.SignalReportStatusEnum Current report status. Monitoring reads as resolved when its rollout is disabled.
---@field monitoring_started_at? string|distilled.Null Original implementation-complete time for this Monitoring period, null before entry. Present only when Monitoring is enabled.
---@field total_weight number
---@field signal_count number
---@field signals_at_run number
---@field collapsed_note_count number How many scout notes this report received beyond the few its work log keeps as entries. 0 when nothing was dropped. These say the finding still holds, so the count is shown in place of the entries.
---@field startup_failure posthog.signals.ReportStartupFailure|distilled.Null Startup failure from the latest failed research attempt, when available.
---@field created_at string
---@field updated_at string
---@field artefact_count number
---@field charts posthog.signals.SignalReportListChartsList Charts the report shows, in the order they were written. The summary places one with a `[label](chart:<chart_id>)` link; the rest render below it.
---@field metrics posthog.signals.SignalReportListMetricsList Snapshot-only impact measurements for inbox rows. Live query definitions and authored comparisons are available from the report detail endpoint.
---@field suggested_prompts posthog.signals.SignalReportListSuggestedPromptsList Follow-up prompts the report's author suggests sending about it (questions to ask, or next-step actions to request), in the order they were written. The inbox offers them above the `Ask AI` box; clicking one fills the box with it.
---@field tags posthog.signals.SignalReportListTagsList Free-form lowercase kebab-case slug tags for grouping and filtering reports, at most 10. Empty when the report has no tags.
---@field source_suggestion posthog.signals.ReportSourceSuggestion|distilled.Null A product the team does not use that would have given this report better evidence, from the latest source suggestion artefact. Null when there is none, or when the team now uses the product. Always null in list responses, because its in-use check can query ClickHouse.
---@field priority string|distilled.Null P0–P4 from the latest priority judgment artefact (when present).
---@field actionability string|distilled.Null Actionability choice from the latest actionability judgment artefact (when present).
---@field already_addressed boolean|distilled.Null Whether the issue is already being handled — fixed in recent changes, or with a fix in flight (an open PR, a recently active branch, an assigned / in-progress issue or agent task) — from the actionability judgment artefact.
---@field dismissal_reason string|distilled.Null Reason code from the latest dismissal artefact, set when the report was suppressed (when present).
---@field dismissal_note string|distilled.Null Free-form note captured alongside the dismissal reason (when present).
---@field suppression_source posthog.signals.SignalReportSuppressionSourceEnum|distilled.Null Who or what suppressed the report. Null unless status is suppressed. `dismissed`: a person or agent dismissed it, it was merged into another report, or its pull request closed without merging; dismissal_reason says which when one was given. `safety_judge`: the safety judge marked it unsafe. `not_actionable`: the actionability judge marked it not actionable. `system`: suppressed by the pipeline for another reason. Every value except `dismissed` is a verdict nobody has reviewed, listed by the `held_back` inbox view.
---@field suppression_explanation string|distilled.Null The judge's explanation when suppression_source is `safety_judge` or `not_actionable`. Null otherwise, or when the judge gave none.
---@field repo_slug string|distilled.Null `organization/repository` the report's work targets, from the latest repo-selection artefact (when present). Lets list cards show repository context without a per-card fetch.
---@field is_self_improvement_report boolean Whether this is a scout self-improvement report. Most update a team-owned skill in the skills store, but reports with a selected repository can still produce a pull request.
---@field research_context posthog.signals.ReportResearchContext|distilled.Null Evidence available to the latest research pass. Null for legacy reports.
---@field is_suggested_reviewer boolean
---@field source_products posthog.signals.SignalReportListSourceProductsList Distinct source products contributing signals to this report (from ClickHouse).
---@field scout_name string|distilled.Null skill_name slug of the scout that authored this report, when scout-authored (from ClickHouse); null otherwise.
---@field implementation_pr_url string|distilled.Null Pull request attached to this report's claim, if available.
---@field pull_requests posthog.signals.SignalReportListPullRequestsList All distinct PRs linked to this report across work attempts.
---@field implementation_pr_state posthog.signals.SignalReportAssignmentPrStateEnum|distilled.Null Latest known pull request state: unknown, draft, open, closed, or merged.
---@field implementation_pr_merged boolean Whether that implementation PR is merged, per the GitHub webhook. False when there is no PR or it hasn't merged. Report status doesn't imply this: a resolved report may have been resolved directly, without a merged PR.
---@field tracker_issue_url string|distilled.Null Link to the issue self-driving opened in the team's tracker for this report's pull request. Null when the team tracks no issues, or the issue could not be opened.
---@field tracker_issue_reference string|distilled.Null How that tracker issue reads in its provider, for example '#12' or 'ENG-123'. Null when there is no tracker issue.
---@field tracker_issue_error string|distilled.Null Why the tracker issue could not be opened, for a team that wants one. Null when the issue exists or the team tracks no issues.
---@field source_issues posthog.signals.SignalReportListSourceIssuesList URLs of the external issues this report is about, as recorded by the scout or person that filed it, oldest first. Normalized to `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<number>`. Empty when the report names none. Issues the report learned about from a GitHub issue signal are not listed here.
---@field work_state posthog.signals.SignalReportWorkStateEnum Derived remediation state: unclaimed, working, in_review, or done.
---@field assignee posthog.signals.SignalReportAssignee|distilled.Null Current user, internal task, or external agent claim owner. Null when unclaimed.
---@field refund posthog.signals.SignalReportRefund|distilled.Null The report's PR refund, when one exists. One refund per report, ever.
---@field refund_ineligibility_reason posthog.signals.RefundIneligibilityReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why refunding this report's PR would be rejected right now, or null when a refund would be accepted (see the field's schema for the reason values).
---@field billing_exempt_reason posthog.signals.SignalReportBillingExemptReasonEnum|distilled.Null Non-null when this report is system-marked never-billable (PostHog-system origin, e.g. a health-check scout finding) — its implementation PRs are free and cannot be refunded because nothing was charged. * `posthog_health_check` - PostHog health check * `posthog_onboarding` - PostHog onboarding * `posthog_system` - PostHog system
---@field channel_id string|distilled.Null The space (task channel) this report is assigned to, or null when unassigned. The general view lists every report regardless of this value.
---@field ranking posthog.signals.ReportRanking The served ranking model's predictions from the latest ranking score artefact. Its status says whether the report is scored, stale or unscored, or that the user cannot see the ranking model.
---@field plan posthog.signals.ReportPlan|distilled.Null The plan this report leads or is a step of, with every step in it. A report that other reports link to with `part_of` is a plan. Null when the report is in no plan, and always null in list responses, because finding a plan's steps costs several queries per report.
---@field inbox_merge_key number|distilled.Null Sort key from the ranker named by the list response's ranker field, for sort=recommended and sort=personal only. Lower keys rank first, so rows from several requests merge in the order of one request. For an outcome ranker (open, action or fix), a scored report gets 1 minus its score, from 0 to 1, and a report without a usable score gets 2 plus its priority rank. The priority ranker uses the priority rank only, from 0 (P0) to 5 (no priority). For the personal ranker, a report in the stored personal ranking gets its position in that ranking from 0, and every other report gets the number of those positions plus its key from the recommended ranker. Null for every other sort.
---@field personal_tier string|distilled.Null The tier your personal ranking gave this report, for sort=personal. Null when the language model did not rank the report, and for every other sort.
---@field personal_reason string|distilled.Null Why your personal ranking put this report where it is, for sort=personal. Null when the language model did not rank the report, and for every other sort.

