---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutCreateResponse
---@field created boolean True when this request created the missing scout skill or config; false when both already existed.
---@field skill posthog.signals.SignalScoutSkillSummary
---@field config posthog.signals.SignalScoutConfig

---One finding a scout run emitted to the inbox — the persisted, queryable record of
---*what* the run surfaced, returned by `scout-runs-emissions-list`. The emitted text
---lives in `description`; `source_id` is the join key (`run:<run_id>:finding:<finding_id>`)
---back into the underlying signal store.
---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutEmission
---@field id string
---@field run_id string UUID of the `SignalScoutRun` that emitted this finding.
---@field finding_id string Stable id the finding was emitted under; matches an entry in the run's `emitted_finding_ids`.
---@field description string The emitted finding prose — the signal's `description` as surfaced to the inbox.
---@field severity posthog.signals.AutonomyPriorityEnum|distilled.Null Optional severity tag — one of P0, P1, P2, P3, P4 — or null if the run didn't set one. * `P0` - P0 * `P1` - P1 * `P2` - P2 * `P3` - P3 * `P4` - P4
---@field tags posthog.signals.SignalScoutEmissionTagsList Slug tags the scout attached to this finding (lowercase kebab-case, e.g. `cost-spike`). Empty list when the run set none.
---@field source_id string Deterministic `run:<run_id>:finding:<finding_id>` — the join key into the underlying signal store.
---@field emitted_at string ISO-8601 timestamp the finding was emitted.

---Slug tags the scout attached to this finding (lowercase kebab-case, e.g. `cost-spike`). Empty list when the run set none.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalScoutEmissionTagsList string[]

---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutOutputDestinations
---@field slack? posthog.signals.SignalScoutSlackDestination|distilled.Null Slack destination for each emitted scout finding or report. Null or omitted disables Slack delivery.
---@field webhook? posthog.signals.SignalScoutWebhookDestination|distilled.Null The CDP destination another product provisioned for this scout's reports. Null or omitted means no webhook. Unlike Slack, Signals does not deliver this itself: the reference lives here so the owning product can manage the destination's lifecycle.
---@field inbox? boolean Whether this scout's reports appear in the shared inbox. Defaults to true. Set false to keep the reports this scout authors out of the inbox and its Slack notifications, for example for a digest scout read in Slack. Reports this scout only edits are not affected. An update that omits this key keeps the stored value.

---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutOutputDestinationsUpdate
---@field slack? posthog.signals.SignalScoutSlackDestinationUpdate|distilled.Null Slack destination for each emitted scout finding or report. Null or omitted disables Slack delivery.
---@field webhook? posthog.signals.SignalScoutWebhookDestination|distilled.Null The CDP destination another product provisioned for this scout's reports. Null or omitted means no webhook. Unlike Slack, Signals does not deliver this itself: the reference lives here so the owning product can manage the destination's lifecycle.
---@field inbox? boolean Whether this scout's reports appear in the shared inbox. Defaults to true. Set false to keep the reports this scout authors out of the inbox and its Slack notifications, for example for a digest scout read in Slack. Reports this scout only edits are not affected. An update that omits this key keeps the stored value.

---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutPrecheckTest
---@field would_run boolean Whether a scheduled run that started now would run the scout. False means it would skip the run.
---@field reason posthog.signals.ScoutPrecheckReasonEnum Why: `rows` (the query found rows), `no_rows` (it found none, so the run is skipped), `false_value` (it returned one false value, so the run is skipped), or `query_error` (the query failed, so the run starts as if there were no pre-check). * `rows` - Rows * `no_rows` - No Rows * `false_value` - False Value * `query_error` - Query Error
---@field since string The value bound to `{since}`: the start of the last run that ran, or when the scout was created.
---@field now string The value bound to `{now}`.
---@field interval_minutes number The value bound to `{interval_minutes}`: the scout's rolling interval, or for a cron schedule the gap in minutes between the fire times around now.
---@field row_count number How many rows the query returned, at most 50.
---@field columns posthog.signals.SignalScoutPrecheckTestColumnsList The column names of the result, in order.
---@field rows_text string The rows as the scout reads them: one JSON object per line, cut before the text passes the size limit. Empty when the query returned no rows or failed.
---@field error string|distilled.Null Why the query failed, when it failed. A syntax or schema error is given as written; other failures read as a general message. Null when the query ran.
---@field acting_user posthog.signals.UserBasic|distilled.Null The member scheduled runs check the query as, when that is not you. The test runs with your access, so a table you can read can still fail on a scheduled run, and the run then starts as if there were no pre-check. Null when scheduled runs check it as you.

---The column names of the result, in order.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalScoutPrecheckTestColumnsList string[]

---Full `SignalScoutRun` projection used by `get-run`. Same shape as the summary
---today; kept distinct so future detail-only extensions (linked Signal rows,
---LLMA token-cost join) can land here without bloating the list response.
---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetail
---@field total_spend number|distilled.Null Accounted customer spend in USD cents, including fractional cents. May be partial; null for untracked runs.
---@field run_id string UUID of the bridge row.
---@field skill_name string Canonical skill name the run executed (e.g. `signals-scout-general`).
---@field skill_version number Skill version snapshotted at run start.
---@field status posthog.signals.RunStatusEnum Status from the linked TaskRun. * `not_started` - not_started * `queued` - queued * `in_progress` - in_progress * `completed` - completed * `failed` - failed * `cancelled` - cancelled
---@field created_at string ISO-8601 timestamp the bridge row was created — the field `date_from` / `date_to` filter and order on. Use this (not `started_at`) as the `date_to` cursor when walking past the 100-row cap, so runs created in the gap between a boundary run's TaskRun and its bridge row aren't skipped.
---@field started_at string ISO-8601 timestamp the TaskRun was created.
---@field completed_at string|distilled.Null ISO-8601 timestamp the TaskRun completed; null while still running.
---@field task_id? string|distilled.Null UUID of the Tasks `Task` the scout span ran inside.
---@field task_run_id? string|distilled.Null UUID of the Tasks `TaskRun`. Pairs with `task_id` to deep-link.
---@field task_url? string|distilled.Null Relative deep-link to the Tasks UI for this run, e.g. `/project/{team_id}/tasks/{task_id}?runId={task_run_id}`.
---@field summary string One-paragraph close-out the scout wrote at end-of-run. Empty string for runs that errored before close-out. The dedupe key for non-emitting runs.
---@field error? string|distilled.Null Full `error_message` from the linked TaskRun, surfaced only for failed/cancelled runs (null otherwise, including on success). Use `failure_reason` for a concise scan-friendly summary.
---@field failure_reason? string|distilled.Null Concise derived reason the run didn't complete cleanly — the first line of `error` (bounded), or a status-derived fallback. Null unless the run terminated failed/cancelled. Read this to see at a glance *why* a run emitted nothing without pulling full stack traces.
---@field emitted_count number Number of findings this run actually emitted to the inbox. 0 for runs that investigated but surfaced nothing, or ran dry-run / before AI approval. `> 0` means the run produced at least one `Signal`.
---@field emitted_finding_ids posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailEmittedFindingIdsList The `finding_id`s behind `emitted_count`, in emit order. Each maps to a `Signal` with `source_id = run:<run_id>:finding:<finding_id>`. Empty for non-emitting runs.
---@field emitted_report_ids posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailEmittedReportIdsList The `SignalReport` ids this run authored directly via the `emit_report` channel, in emit order. Separate from `emitted_finding_ids` (weak `emit_signal` findings) — a report-authoring scout writes a full report here instead. Empty for runs that authored no report.
---@field edited_report_ids posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailEditedReportIdsList The `SignalReport` ids this run mutated via the `edit_report` channel (rewrote title/summary and/or appended a note), deduped. Distinct from `emitted_report_ids`: edit can target any inbox report, so these are generally not reports the run authored. Empty for runs that edited no report.
---@field metadata posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailMetadata Scout-owned per-run context, in two regions. Top-level keys are stamped by the runner at run start. Always present: `harness_prompt_version` (id of the harness prompt build the run was given), `report_channel` (which report tools the run held: `none`, `emit`, `edit`, or `both`), `skill_origin` (`canonical` or `custom`), `github_guidance` (whether the run got the GitHub evidence section), and `business_knowledge_maintained` (whether the run got the business-knowledge section: the product flag is on and the team's knowledge base looks maintained) — the provenance set that says which instructions the run actually got, so runs are only compared against runs of the same shape. Present only when the run departed from a default: `model`, `runtime_adapter`, and `reasoning_effort` (routing overrode the agent-server default), `network_access` (`full` when the scout's config lifted the trusted-domain network restriction for this run), `write_scopes` (the extra write access the run's token carried, when the scout was granted any), and `triggered_by` (`manual` or `workflow` when the run was fired off-schedule; absent means the run came from the coordinator's schedule). The nested `derived` object is the harness's own map of boolean run dimensions, computed server-side at finalize: `has_emit_report`, `has_edit_report`, `has_self_improvement`, `has_chart`, `has_self_validation`, `has_structured_output`, and `has_not_in_use_closeout` (the run wrote a `not-in-use:` scratchpad entry and produced no report, finding, or structured output). Use `derived` to answer 'what kind of run was this?' instead of parsing the `summary` prose. Note the flags describe the reports the run authored as they stand now, so charts attached to someone else's report via an edit are not counted. A missing `derived` object is unknown, not all-false: the run predates the field, never finalized, or its stamp failed.

---The `SignalReport` ids this run mutated via the `edit_report` channel (rewrote title/summary and/or appended a note), deduped. Distinct from `emitted_report_ids`: edit can target any inbox report, so these are generally not reports the run authored. Empty for runs that edited no report.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailEditedReportIdsList string[]

---The `finding_id`s behind `emitted_count`, in emit order. Each maps to a `Signal` with `source_id = run:<run_id>:finding:<finding_id>`. Empty for non-emitting runs.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailEmittedFindingIdsList string[]

---The `SignalReport` ids this run authored directly via the `emit_report` channel, in emit order. Separate from `emitted_finding_ids` (weak `emit_signal` findings) — a report-authoring scout writes a full report here instead. Empty for runs that authored no report.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunDetailEmittedReportIdsList string[]

---Scout-owned per-run context, in two regions. Top-level keys are stamped by the runner at run start. Always present: `harness_prompt_version` (id of the harness prompt build the run was given), `report_channel` (which report tools the run held: `none`, `emit`, `edit`, or `both`), `skill_origin` (`canonical` or `custom`), `github_guidance` (whether the run got the GitHub evidence section), and `business_knowledge_maintained` (whether the run got the business-knowledge section: the product flag is on and the team's knowledge base looks maintained) — the provenance set that says which instructions the run actually got, so runs are only compared against runs of the same shape. Present only when the run departed from a default: `model`, `runtime_adapter`, and `reasoning_effort` (routing overrode the agent-server default), `network_access` (`full` when the scout's config lifted the trusted-domain network restriction for this run), `write_scopes` (the extra write access the run's token carried, when the scout was granted any), and `triggered_by` (`manual` or `workflow` when the run was fired off-schedule; absent means the run came from the coordinator's schedule). The nested `derived` object is the harness's own map of boolean run dimensions, computed server-side at finalize: `has_emit_report`, `has_edit_report`, `has_self_improvement`, `has_chart`, `has_self_validation`, `has_structured_output`, and `has_not_in_use_closeout` (the run wrote a `not-in-use:` scratchpad entry and produced no report, finding, or structured output). Use `derived` to answer 'what kind of run was this?' instead of parsing the `summary` prose. Note the flags describe the reports the run authored as they stand now, so charts attached to someone else's report via an edit are not counted. A missing `derived` object is unknown, not all-false: the run predates the field, never finalized, or its stamp failed.
