---Status and timestamps flow from the linked `tasks.TaskRun`.
---@class posthog.signals.SignalScoutRunSummary
---@field total_spend number|distilled.Null Accounted customer spend in USD cents, including fractional cents. May be partial; null for untracked runs.
---@field run_id string UUID of the bridge row.
---@field skill_name string Canonical skill name the run executed (e.g. `signals-scout-general`).
---@field skill_version number Skill version snapshotted at run start.
---@field status posthog.signals.RunStatusEnum Status from the linked TaskRun. * `not_started` - not_started * `queued` - queued * `in_progress` - in_progress * `completed` - completed * `failed` - failed * `cancelled` - cancelled
---@field created_at string ISO-8601 timestamp the bridge row was created — the field `date_from` / `date_to` filter and order on. Use this (not `started_at`) as the `date_to` cursor when walking past the 100-row cap, so runs created in the gap between a boundary run's TaskRun and its bridge row aren't skipped.
---@field started_at string ISO-8601 timestamp the TaskRun was created.
---@field completed_at string|distilled.Null ISO-8601 timestamp the TaskRun completed; null while still running.
---@field task_id? string|distilled.Null UUID of the Tasks `Task` the scout span ran inside.
---@field task_run_id? string|distilled.Null UUID of the Tasks `TaskRun`. Pairs with `task_id` to deep-link.
---@field task_url? string|distilled.Null Relative deep-link to the Tasks UI for this run, e.g. `/project/{team_id}/tasks/{task_id}?runId={task_run_id}`.
