---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field run_id string UUID of the `SignalScoutRun` bridge row.
---@field description string Canonical evidence-bundle prose. Becomes the signal's `description`.
---@field evidence posthog.signals.SignalSignalsScoutEmitRequestEvidenceList Citations supporting the finding. Capped at 20 entries.
---@field hypothesis? string|distilled.Null Optional one-line hypothesis the finding tests.
---@field severity? posthog.signals.AutonomyPriorityEnum|string|distilled.Null Optional severity tag — one of P0, P1, P2, P3, P4. Informational only. * `P0` - P0 * `P1` - P1 * `P2` - P2 * `P3` - P3 * `P4` - P4
---@field dedupe_keys? posthog.signals.SignalSignalsScoutEmitRequestDedupeKeysList Optional keys for downstream dedupe (e.g. `error_tracking_issue:<id>`).
---@field tags? posthog.signals.SignalSignalsScoutEmitRequestTagsList Optional category tags as lowercase kebab-case slugs (e.g. `cost-spike`, `silent-failure`), max 10. Reuse the vocabulary in your `tags:<domain>:taxonomy` scratchpad entry when a tag fits; coin a new slug when a genuinely new category emerges. Near-miss formats are normalized to slugs; persisted in the signal's `extra.tags` and on the emission row.
---@field time_range? posthog.signals.TimeRange|distilled.Null Optional time window the finding refers to.
---@field mcp_trace_id? string|distilled.Null Optional MCP trace id for cross-system debugging.
---@field finding_id? string|distilled.Null Stable id for this finding, baked into the signal's source_id for traceability. NOT a dedupe key — re-emitting the same id creates another signal.

