---@class posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfig
---@field id string
---@field autostart_enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Master switch for autonomous inbox PRs. Null (never set) leaves autostart on; set false to opt out, so actionable reports still generate and notify but the team never auto-starts an implementation task or opens a PR — reviewers open PRs manually.
---@field default_autostart_priority? posthog.signals.AutonomyPriorityEnum
---@field default_slack_notification_channel? string|distilled.Null Default Slack channel for this team's signal inbox notifications, in the same `channel_id|#channel-name` shape PostHog uses elsewhere (only the channel id is required). Null means no team-level default; per-user channels still apply.
---@field default_slack_notification_integration? number|distilled.Null Connected Slack integration that owns `default_slack_notification_channel`. Send it together with the channel. A channel saved without it is routed through the team's oldest Slack integration, and clearing the channel clears this too.
---@field autostart_base_branches? posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfigAutostartBaseBranchesMap Per-repository base branch overrides for auto-started inbox PRs, keyed by 'organization/repository'. The branch is what the auto-PR targets; omit a repo (or send {}) to keep targeting the repo default branch.
---@field scout_instructions? string Project-level instructions added to every scout run, alongside project instructions and the scout's own brief. Blank uses project instructions only.
---@field research_instructions? string Project-level instructions for the dedicated signal report research stage. Other agent roles do not receive them. Blank uses project instructions only.
---@field implementation_instructions? string Project-level instructions for agents implementing signal reports. Other agent roles do not receive them. Blank uses project instructions only.
---@field issue_tracking_integration? number|distilled.Null Connected GitHub, GitLab, Linear, or Jira integration that self-driving opens a tracker issue in for each pull request it makes. Null turns tracker issues off, which is the default.
---@field issue_tracking_config? posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfigIssueTrackingConfigMap Where in the tracker the issues land. Required keys depend on the integration kind: github -> {repository}; linear -> {team_id}; jira -> {project_key}; gitlab needs none, because its integration is already bound to one project. An optional 'label' is applied to created GitHub issues.
---@field max_reports_per_day? number|distilled.Null Daily cap on new reports surfacing to the inbox, counted per calendar day in the project's timezone. Once reached, signal ingestion, scout runs, and report research pause until local midnight. Null means unlimited.
---@field default_open_pull_request_ready? boolean Whether self-driving pull requests open ready for review instead of draft, so the full CI matrix starts when the pull request is created. False by default. A reviewer's own github_open_pull_request_ready overrides this for reports that suggest them as reviewer.
---@field github_issue_writeback_enabled? boolean Whether self-driving comments back on a GitHub issue that raised a report, linking to the report so everybody watching the issue knows it is being researched. The comment is public on the issue thread and carries a link only, never report content. False by default. Needs a GitHub integration that can reach the issue's repository.
---@field pull_request_label_enabled? boolean Whether self-driving adds a label to every pull request it opens, so GitHub search, saved searches, and notification rules can separate them from other automation on the repository. False by default. Needs a GitHub integration that can reach the repository.
---@field pull_request_label? string|distilled.Null The label name self-driving applies, at most 50 characters. Null or blank means 'self-driving'. The label is created in the repository when it does not exist yet. Only used while pull_request_label_enabled is true.
---@field implementation_repositories? posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfigImplementationRepositoriesList Extra GitHub repositories, as 'organization/repository', that self-driving implementation tasks can read and write within the connected GitHub App's permissions, for example an assets repository for PR screenshots. A task gets only the entries with the same owner as its selected repository. They are not cloned, and the PR still targets the selected repository. Each new entry must be reachable through one of the project's GitHub installations. Changes apply to tasks started afterwards. Empty by default.
---@field anomaly_scoring_enabled? boolean Whether anomaly scoring runs while the Product analytics source (analytics / anomaly_investigation) is on. Scoring checks this project's active trends insights for anomalies and writes the results as $anomaly_score events, which are not billed. True by default. False stops new scores and keeps alert signals; events written before stay. Turning the source off stops scoring whatever this value is, and turning the source on again keeps this value. Turning it on does not enroll a project that anomaly_scoring_available reports as not covered.
---@field anomaly_scoring_available boolean Whether the anomaly scoring rollout covers this project. PostHog decides which projects it covers. A covered project is scored only while its Product analytics source is on.
---@field reports_generated_today number How many reports first became visible in the inbox during the current project-timezone day. This is the count the daily report limit compares against.
---@field daily_report_limit_reached boolean Whether the team hit its daily report limit, pausing new report generation until local midnight. Always false when max_reports_per_day is null.
---@field created_at string
---@field updated_at string

---Per-repository base branch overrides for auto-started inbox PRs, keyed by 'organization/repository'. The branch is what the auto-PR targets; omit a repo (or send {}) to keep targeting the repo default branch.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfigAutostartBaseBranchesMap { [string]: string }

---Extra GitHub repositories, as 'organization/repository', that self-driving implementation tasks can read and write within the connected GitHub App's permissions, for example an assets repository for PR screenshots. A task gets only the entries with the same owner as its selected repository. They are not cloned, and the PR still targets the selected repository. Each new entry must be reachable through one of the project's GitHub installations. Changes apply to tasks started afterwards. Empty by default.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfigImplementationRepositoriesList string[]

---Where in the tracker the issues land. Required keys depend on the integration kind: github -> {repository}; linear -> {team_id}; jira -> {project_key}; gitlab needs none, because its integration is already bound to one project. An optional 'label' is applied to created GitHub issues.
---@alias posthog.signals.SignalTeamConfigIssueTrackingConfigMap { [string]: string }

---@class posthog.signals.SignalsAnomaliesSearchRetrieveRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field dashboard_id? number Only the series of the insights on this dashboard, by numeric id.
---@field date_from? string Earliest bucket start in the range. A relative date such as `-7d` or `-24h`, or an ISO 8601 date.
---@field date_to? string Latest bucket start in the range. A relative date or an ISO 8601 date. Defaults to now.
---@field group_by? posthog.signals.SignalsAnomaliesSearchRetrieveRequestGroupBy|string `series` returns one row per series in `series`. `insight` returns one row per insight in `insights`. * `series` - Series * `insight` - Insight
---@field insight_id? number Only the series of this insight, by numeric id.
---@field interval? posthog.signals.SignalsAnomaliesSearchRetrieveRequestInterval|string Only series with this interval. * `hour` - Hour * `day` - Day * `week` - Week * `month` - Month
---@field limit? number The most rows to return.
---@field only_flagged? boolean Only series, or insights, with at least one flagged bucket in the range. Set false to also list quiet ones.

---@alias posthog.signals.SignalsAnomaliesSearchRetrieveRequestGroupBy "series"|"insight"

---@alias posthog.signals.SignalsAnomaliesSearchRetrieveRequestInterval "hour"|"day"|"week"|"month"

