---One suggested reviewer — identified by `github_login`, `user_uuid`, or both.
---
---A reviewer is a PostHog user, so a `user_uuid` only has to name an org member of this team: a
---member with no linked GitHub account routes the report like anyone else. A `user_uuid` that
---isn't an org member of this team is rejected — so a reviewer is never silently dropped.
---@class posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewer
---@field github_login? string GitHub login (case-insensitive, stored lowercased) — e.g. `octocat`, no `@`, no display name. Resolve one via `scout-members-list` (each member row carries a resolved `github_login`) or git history when you only have a name.
---@field user_uuid? string PostHog user UUID (e.g. from `scout-members-list`, or an entity's `created_by`). Use this when you know the PostHog user, whether or not they have a GitHub handle — every member is routable this way. Must be a concrete UUID; the `@me` alias is not valid here.
---@field reason? string|distilled.Null One sentence of evidence for WHY this person: what ties them to the affected surface (e.g. 'authored 4 of the last 10 commits touching products/tracing/mcp/', 'human correction routed the prior tracing report to them'). Persisted on the report so the routing is auditable — always set it when you can name the evidence; 'precedent' alone is weak, prefer code-derived ownership.

---Commit evidence behind a suggested reviewer.
---@class posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewerCommit
---@field sha string Commit SHA.
---@field url string Link to the commit.
---@field reason string Why the commit makes this reviewer relevant.

---One reviewer as the read path returns it: the stored entry plus read-time enrichment.
---
---`source_label`, `explanation` and `user` are computed on read, not stored, so a caller cannot
---write them.
---@class posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewerEntryRead
---@field github_login string|distilled.Null GitHub login, lowercased. Null when the reviewer has no linked account.
---@field user_uuid string|distilled.Null PostHog user this entry routes to. Null on entries written before reviewers had one.
---@field github_name string|distilled.Null Display name, when the writer supplied one.
---@field relevant_commits posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewerEntryReadRelevantCommitsList Commits attributed to this reviewer. Empty when the pick came from elsewhere.
---@field reason string|distilled.Null Why this reviewer was chosen.
---@field is_skill_owner boolean True when the scout owner guardrail added the entry rather than commit authorship.
---@field is_default_owner boolean True when no evidence selected anyone and the report fell back to the project's default owner. The entry routes the report, but it is not ownership evidence.
---@field source_skill string|distilled.Null Scout skill whose run wrote the entry. Null when no scout did.
---@field source_label string Where the suggestion came from, for display.
---@field explanation string|distilled.Null One line of evidence for display. Null when there is none to show.
---@field user posthog.signals.User|distilled.Null Resolved org member. Null when the entry resolves to nobody.

---Commits attributed to this reviewer. Empty when the pick came from elsewhere.
---@alias posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewerEntryReadRelevantCommitsList posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewerCommit[]

---Single entry in a PUT body for a `suggested_reviewers` artefact.
---
---Each entry must identify a reviewer by at least one of `github_login` or `user_uuid`. A
---`user_uuid` only has to name an org member on this team — a member with no linked GitHub
---account is stored by uuid and routes like any other reviewer.
---@class posthog.signals.SuggestedReviewerEntryWrite
---@field github_login? string GitHub login (case-insensitive). Stored lowercased. Required unless `user_uuid` is given.
---@field user_uuid? string PostHog user UUID. Must be an org member on this team; a linked GitHub account is not required. Required unless `github_login` is given. If supplied together with `github_login`, the user's own identity wins.
---@field github_name? string Optional human-readable display name. Not backfilled from GitHub by the server.
---@field reason? string|distilled.Null Optional short evidence for why this reviewer was chosen. Omitted entries keep the prior reason for reviewers already on the report.

